    <h2>What Studio Actually Adds (In Detail)</h2>

    <h3>1. Neural Engine AI Tools</h3>
    <p>Studio unlocks the full DaVinci Neural Engine suite:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Magic Mask</strong> — automatically tracks and masks a person/object without manual rotoscoping. Click once, it follows the subject through the clip.</li>
        <li><strong>Super Scale</strong> — AI upscaling for low-res footage (useful for old client footage or social media re-purposing).</li>
        <li><strong>Face Refinement</strong> — subtle facial retouching directly in the Color page, node-based (no plugin needed).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2. GPU Noise Reduction</h3>
    <p>Studio's <strong>Temporal + Spatial NR</strong> and <strong>UltraNR</strong> run on GPU acceleration — critical if you shoot in low light (common in Haryanvi/Rajasthani music video night shoots) and need clean grades without crushing detail.</p>

    <h3>3. HDR Grading</h3>
    <p>Full HDR (Dolby Vision, HDR10) grading tools — relevant if you're delivering to OTT platforms or high-end brand campaigns.</p>

    <h3>4. Multi-GPU & Higher Resolution</h3>
    <p>Free version caps at 4K/60fps. Studio unlocks higher frame rates (120fps) and resolutions — needed for high-end commercial/cinema delivery, not typical for YouTube/Instagram content.</p>

